A rectangle has area $91\text{ cm}^2$ and length $13\text{ cm}$. Find its width.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (13,7);
\path (6.5,0) node[below] {$13\text{ cm}$};
\path (13,3.5) node[right] {width};
\path (6.5,3.5) node {$91\text{ cm}^2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Compare the areas and perimeters of rectangles $18\text{ cm}$ by $5\text{ cm}$ and $15\text{ cm}$ by $6\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.5mm,y=2.5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (18,5);
\path (9,0) node[below] {$18\text{ cm}$};
\path (18,2.5) node[right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw[black] (27,0) rectangle (42,6);
\path (34.5,0) node[below] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\path (42,3) node[right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Compare the perimeters and areas of rectangles $23\text{ m}$ by $4\text{ m}$ and $16\text{ m}$ by $11\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.5mm,y=2.5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (23,4);
\path (11.5,0) node[below] {$23\text{ m}$};
\path (23,2) node[right] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[black] (32,0) rectangle (48,11);
\path (40,0) node[below] {$16\text{ m}$};
\path (48,5.5) node[right] {$11\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
